# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# dust/uninstall-coq-toolchain.a2ml — Cleanup intention: remove Coq toolchain
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# Verb: dust
# Scope: my-lang Coq mechanised solo-core
# Cleanup intention: cleanly detach / uninstall the Coq proof infrastructure
#   if the project pivots to a different proof assistant or moves to Idris2-only

@abstract:
How to cleanly remove the Coq mechanised solo-core from my-lang if the project
pivots (e.g., to Idris2-only, or to a new proof assistant). This does NOT
retire the formal verification commitment — it details what must be removed,
what must be preserved, and what downstream consumers must be informed of.
@end

## Cleanup Intention

### scope
- description: Remove the Coq toolchain, CI leg, and Coq-specific source
- trigger: Deliberate architectural pivot away from Coq as the canonical mechanisation
- authority: Requires explicit sign-off in GOVERNANCE.adoc; not a unilateral CI fix

## Steps

### 1-archive-coq-proofs
- description: Move proofs/verification/coq/ to an archive branch, not delete
- run: "git archive HEAD proofs/verification/coq/ | gzip > /tmp/my-lang-coq-archive.tar.gz"
- notes: The Coq proofs are the F1.4 canonical; they must be retrievable for audit

### 2-disable-proofs-ci
- description: Remove or gate .github/workflows/proofs.yml Coq steps
- run: "rm .github/workflows/proofs.yml || sed -i '/coqc\\|coq_makefile/d' .github/workflows/proofs.yml"
- notes: Preserve Idris2 CI leg if Idris2-only route is chosen

### 3-remove-coq-project-files
- description: Remove _CoqProject and CoqMakefile
- run: "rm -f proofs/verification/coq/solo-core/_CoqProject proofs/verification/coq/solo-core/CoqMakefile"

### 4-update-guix-manifest
- description: Remove coq / coq-mathcomp entries from guix.scm
- run: "grep -n 'coq' guix.scm && echo 'Review and remove the above lines manually'"
- severity: advisory

### 5-update-6a2-state
- description: Update STATE.a2ml and META.a2ml to reflect Coq retirement
- corrective: >
    In 6a2/STATE.a2ml: mark coq_core as retired; in 6a2/META.a2ml: remove
    ADR-009 (open-context subst) as Coq-specific or generalise it.

### 6-notify-downstream
- description: Notify nextgen-languages, nextgen-typing, echo-types of Coq retirement
- corrective: >
    File an issue in each downstream repo linking to the archive branch.
    Update docs/design/echo-types-integration.md to note the Coq bridge is archived.

## Completion Criteria
- run: "test ! -f .github/workflows/proofs.yml || ! grep -q 'coqc' .github/workflows/proofs.yml"
- severity: advisory
